{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793397493,"nonce":"gH7GGiz8dDJRxxWuKESxFJ/gtss=","title":"Site web bundle rebuilt against ashui e9cd805 answers extension host requests late, so the rayzor LSP never registers","message":"Rebuilding site/dist with scripts/build-site.sh against the pin moved to ashui e9cd805 (commit 1e33956; was 3f07c51) makes the browser editor service the extension host's calls slowly. Symptom: the status bar shows Preparing extensions and Rayzor starting, then the host is killed and respawned about every 60 s (starting and restarting), and rayzor lsp is never launched.\n\nMeasured with headless Chrome logging every WebSocket frame, against sessions started from the same rayde-session, extension host and workspace copy, varying only the bundle:\n- old committed bundle (HEAD before the rebuild): the page answers the rayzor extension's rayde.settings.get within about 50 ms, rayde.languages.registerServer follows at 2.24 s, rayzor lsp is spawned at 2.28 s and indexing output arrives by 2.6 s.\n- rebuilt bundle: the first page reply comes at about 5 s and the next at about 15 s (bursts, roughly every 10 s), registerServer is not reached within 30 s, and the same pattern repeats after the host is respawned at 62 s. The git extension's rayde.workspace.root call stalls the same way.\nThe same stall reproduces against the long-running 8731 preview session, so it is not a stale browser tab.\n\nRuled out: rayzor lsp itself (initialize in 20-140 ms directly and through a live session, by absolute path and by bare name; binary unchanged until rayzor-34 rebuilt it at 21:57, and the rebuilt one is just as fast), the session and extension host binaries (identical in both runs), the Ash runtime used for linking (Oct 29, unchanged), and any hand-built session setup.\n\nNot yet known: which side is at fault. The bundles differ by the 19 ashui commits between the two pins and RayDE's own commits since (surface preview code, Workbench, EditorPart, RunPart, ShellPart). Plan: build old RayDE source against the new pin and new source against the old pin to split the two, then bisect the ashui range. ashui has a host-call path to check: the page seems to service host calls only on a slow wake cadence, so look at idle and wake behaviour in the window loop and Work.notify for background-thread input.\n\nInterim: git checkout -- site/dist restores the working committed bundle; the pin change may need reverting until this is understood. The rebuilt bundle is uncommitted.","files":null}]}